happy holidays it's the official  gift-giving season of the year if you  think kids need Santa Claus think of all  the adults out there who are about to  live off ramen for the next six months  just so that they can pay for all those  gifts thankfully I've come up with a  cheaper tastier and more thoughtful  approach to gift-giving this season  check out my top 3 DIY holiday gifts for  the foodies on your list first up my  sweet and spicy almonds in a medium bowl  I whisk together an egg white and water  until frothy and mix with some blanched  almonds in another bowl I combined some  brown sugar and yummy spices and toss  the almonds in until they're coated well  spread the almond mixture onto a  prepared baking sheet in an even layer  and sprinkle with fleur de sel then  place in the oven and bake for 25 to 30  minutes at 300 degrees stirring at least  halfway room when it's time to gift add  a personal touch with one of these cute  name tags then take a recycled nut  container remove the label and cover it  with festive paper then insert a  cellophane bag and fill it with your  spiced nuts finish with some pretty  ribbon and enjoy next my orange rosemary  olives in a small saucepan I heat some  olive oil with garlic some strips of  orange zest grated orange zest and a  whole rosemary sprig over medium heat  for 5 minutes then I pour the olive oil  mixture over some mixed olives and pack  it into a glass jar top the lid with  some holiday paper and something fun  like this pine cone I found on the side  of the road wrap in some pretty ribbon  and fasten with some olive forks for  easy access and finally my four seasons  chocolate bark pour some melted dark  chocolate into a baking sheet lined with  a nonstick nap then get creative I  couldn't decide so I made for different  flavor combos one corner I added minced  ginger cranberries gingersnaps and  pistachios on the other I did candy  canes and white chocolate drizzle then I  did freeze dried fruit almonds pink  peppercorns and some salt and finally  some golden raisins sesame seeds pine  and candied lemon to gift-wrap I add  some pretty ribbon and fasten a bow  along with a crab mallet to smash your  chocolate bark these gifts are so  delicious easy and inexpensive to pull  off you'll have enough for both your  nice and naughty list happy holidays  guys from my kitchen to yours we're  great healthy holiday ideas be sure to  subscribe to my channel and I'll see you  next time Abby station
 

